---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Hipotecalc"
  description="Hipotecalc privacy policy: what data is processed, for what purpose, and how to exercise your rights under the GDPR."
  heading="Privacy policy"
  path="/en/privacy-policy"
  lang="en"
  lastUpdated="July 2026"
>
  <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
  <p>
    The controller of the personal data collected through this website is the
    owner of <strong>hipotecalc.com</strong>. You can contact them about any
    matter relating to this policy through the contact channels available on
    the website.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What data we process</h2>
  <p>Hipotecalc is designed to collect as little data as possible:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No registration required.</strong> No name, email address or any
      other identifying information is requested to use the calculators.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Calculations run in your browser.</strong> The figures you enter
      in the calculators (prices, savings, age, family situation, etc.) are
      not sent to our servers or stored.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Browsing and analytics data.</strong> Only if you accept
      analytics cookies, statistical usage data is collected (pages visited,
      device type, visit duration) through Google Analytics, with the IP
      address anonymised.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Purpose and legal basis</h2>
  <p>
    Statistical browsing data is processed for the sole purpose of
    understanding how the website is used and improving its content and
    operation. The legal basis for this processing is your
    <strong>consent</strong> (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR), requested through the cookie
    banner, which you can withdraw at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Data retention</h2>
  <p>
    Analytics data is retained for the standard periods defined by the
    analytics tool (up to a maximum of 14 months) and is then deleted or
    aggregated in a way that no longer identifies the user.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Recipients and international transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Statistical data is processed by Google Analytics (Google Ireland Ltd.) as
    data processor. This service may involve international data transfers
    covered by the safeguards provided for in the GDPR, such as standard
    contractual clauses or applicable adequacy frameworks. Personal data is
    never sold or shared with third parties for commercial purposes.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You may at any time exercise your rights of access, rectification,
    erasure, objection, restriction of processing and portability recognised
    by the GDPR and Spanish Organic Law 3/2018 (LOPDGDD) by contacting the
    site owner through the website's contact channels. You also have the right
    to lodge a complaint with the
    <a href="https://www.aepd.es/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Spanish Data Protection Agency (AEPD)</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Detailed information about the cookies used and how to manage them is
    available in the <a href="/en/cookie-policy">cookie policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    This policy may be updated to reflect regulatory or website changes. The
    date of the latest revision is shown at the top of this page.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
